brussels the capital of belgium and home  to more than a million people  for many it's also the world's chocolate  capital  the place to grandson is lined with the  shops of nearly all the country's top  chocolatiers  among them pierre marcolini  he gives us a warm welcome at eight in  the morning  hello nice to meet you thank you very  much  pierre keeps a busy schedule this  afternoon he'll be off to paris for a tv  interview but first it's time for  breakfast chocolate of course  makolini says he eats up bars worth  every day  i always tell people  when you eat our chocolate at home  take out a piece  and put it down somewhere  then close the packet and put it as far  away as possible  then go ahead and eat your piece  and if you don't do this you'll eat the  entire packet  this is mainly milk chocolate with a bit  of caramel and butter it's absolutely  addictive  this is the second time we've met pierre  we take a look at the report from our  first encounter  pierre has always been something of an  enfonterible in the culinary community  by the time we met in 2007 his  experimental creations had already won  him many accolades such as world pastry  champion  today he's considered one of the world's  best chocolatiers  his creations are sold in dozens of  specialty boutiques from hong kong to  new york  we set out for a tour through the salon  district it's a true insider's guide all  of his favorite spots are in this  neighborhood  notre dame  is a lovely example of gothic  architecture dating back to the 15th  century  right next door is the petit sablan park  an oasis of calm in the midst of the  bustling city  the district is a paradise for shoppers  looking for a special keepsake  nearly every corner has an antique shop  gallery or specialty boutique  like ogrondraswan one of pierre's  favorites  there's an unmatched selection of  straight razors and shaving kits from  around the world a perfectionist himself  pierre appreciates the quality on  display here and the owner's expertise  next we pay a visit to the gallery run  by patrick  which sells traditional artifacts from  all over the world  just a few days ago pierre bought a 200  year old wooden spear a wonderful  example of the craftsmanship he values  so  on this highly  this is what sablong is all about  there are so many unique things here in  places like the shaving shop in this  gallery  there's an excellent selection  everywhere  with knowledgeable advice expertise  the atomium is a popular tourist  destination as is the european  parliament  but we keep going  pierre wants to show me more of his  neighborhood  this building is another favorite it's  named old england the aunt nouveau  building is more than a century old once  a department store today it houses the  city's musical instrument  museum this luxury car dealership has a  surprise in store an in-house bar and  bistro  called why it's the latest project by  michelin star chef bart depotter it's a  place to get a quick bite without  skimping on quality  i enjoy a good meal just as much as i  enjoy a new chocolate  it's two in the afternoon  when we're done with lunch pierre  mcelini will leave for his interview in  paris  it's all in a day's work for one of the  world's most sought-after chocolatiers  from brussels
 

